  "operatingHours": "Suzhou Metro (Lines 1–8 and 11) runs ~5:40–6:00 AM to ~10:30–11:00 PM depending on line and station, often 20–40 min later on Fridays, weekends and holidays; trains every 3–8 min by day. No all-night service.",
  "fareInfo": "Distance-based fares from ¥2; most city trips ¥3–5 (2026). Easiest for visitors: scan the Suzhou Metro QR code in Alipay or WeChat (foreign Visa/Mastercard can be linked), or buy a single-journey ticket with cash or QR at station machines; T-Union transit cards also work, and 1-day/3-day tourist passes are sold. Bag checks at every station. Suzhou has no passenger airport: most international visitors fly into Shanghai Hongqiao (SHA), walk to Hongqiao Railway Station and take a G/D train to Suzhou, Suzhou North or Suzhou Industrial Park (~20–30 min, ~¥25–40, every few minutes), or fly into Shanghai Pudong (PVG) and transfer to Hongqiao (Metro Line 2, ~1 h 15 min) or take a direct coach to Suzhou (~2–3 h). Suzhou Metro Line 11 also links Kunshan to Shanghai Metro Line 11 at Huaqiao.",
